# MinIO objects

## Gate

Use when the user asks to list objects, read metadata/tags/versions,
upload/download/copy, ask about an object, write text into an object, or
mint a short-lived presigned URL on a MinIO MCP surface. Skip bare "S3"
for another store. Always load `minio-safety` with this rule.

Never invent a bucket name or object key. Resolve from MCP listing this
turn or from names the user pasted.

## Prefer MCP (dual namespaces)

Same tool surface on both live MinIO MCPs. Pick **one** per turn:

| User signal | Prefer namespace |
| --- | --- |
| swarm / fleet / primary | `user-mcp_minio_swarm` |
| backup / DR / secondary | `user-mcp_minio_backup` |
| ambiguous | ask once, or use the only ready namespace |

Do not invent a side CLI while MCP works.

| Need | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| List objects | `list_bucket_contents` | `bucket_name`; optional `prefix`, `recursive`, `with_metadata`, `with_versions` |
| Object metadata | `get_object_metadata` | `bucket_name` + `object_name` |
| Object tags (read) | `get_object_tags` | |
| Object tags (write) | `set_object_tags` | `tags` JSON string; optional `version_id` |
| Object versions | `get_object_versions` | after versioning is on |
| Ask about object | `ask_object` | `question` about a resolved object |
| Download | `download_object` | `file_path` local; optional `version_id` |
| Upload | `upload_object` | `file_path` + `object_name`; overwrite-gated |
| Text → object | `text_to_object` | optional `content_type` (default text/plain) |
| Copy | `copy_object` | src/dst bucket + object; optional `version_id` |
| Presigned URL | `get_object_presigned_url` | `expires` seconds (tool often requires it) |
| Allowed local dirs | `list_allowed_directories` | before upload/download paths |
| Local files | `list_local_files` | under an allowed path |

## Discover first

1. Resolve bucket (`list_buckets` or user-pasted name) on the chosen MCP.
2. `list_bucket_contents` with a tight `prefix` when the keyspace is large;
   set `recursive` only when needed.

## Prefix pagination

1. Start with a narrow prefix the user named; widen one segment at a time.
2. Use `with_metadata` when size or headers matter; avoid recursive listing
   on huge buckets until a prefix is justified.
3. When the tool returns a truncated page, say so and offer the next prefix
   — do not assume an empty bucket from a partial page.
3. Prefer `with_versions` / `get_object_versions` when the ask is about
   history or a specific version.
4. If several keys match a fuzzy ask, list candidates and ask once.

## Read paths

1. Metadata / tags / versions: call the matching get tool on a resolved
   bucket + key.
2. `ask_object`: use for grounded Q&A about object content the MCP can
   read — still redact secrets in the chat reply (`minio-safety`).
3. Presigned URL: pass an explicit `expires` (seconds). Report expiry and
   that the URL is time-limited — do not treat it as a long-lived
   credential dump to paste broadly.

## Transfer paths (upload / download / copy / text)

1. Before local paths: `list_allowed_directories`, then `list_local_files`
   when the file name is unclear.
2. Download: `download_object` to an allowed `file_path`; optional
   `version_id` from a prior versions list.
3. Upload: `upload_object` with resolved bucket + `object_name` +
   `file_path`. Overwriting an existing key needs an explicit verb
   (`minio-safety`).
4. Text write: `text_to_object` — same overwrite gate; prefer
   `content_type` when not plain text.
5. Copy: resolve both src and dst bucket/key; optional `version_id` on
   source. Cross-MCP copy is out of scope unless the user named both
   endpoints and both MCPs are ready — prefer same-namespace copy.

## Report shape

- MCP namespace used
- Bucket + object key (+ version id when used)
- Action (list / get / upload / download / copy / ask / presign)
- Short finding (size, last-modified, tag keys, local path) — no access
  keys, no secret object bodies

## Out of scope

- Bucket create / lifecycle / replication / admin — see `minio-buckets`
- Delete / public ACL / credential paste — see `minio-safety`
- Inventing delete tools that are not on the live MCP

